# share/keys - what each mux key binding does, for `mux keys` and prefix-?.
#
# DATA, not a second copy of the bindings. The bindings live in `share/mux.tmux`
# and nothing here rebinds anything; this file only names them. The suite checks
# BOTH directions -- every key the fragment binds must be described here, and
# every key described here must be bound there -- so the cheat sheet cannot
# quietly drift from the keys it claims to document. That is the same failure
# `mux check` was built to catch one layer down: a list written by hand stops
# growing with the features.
#
# Format: KEY<TAB>one line, imperative, no trailing full stop. Lines starting
# with `#` and blank lines are ignored. The order here is the order shown, so it
# is grouped by what you reach for rather than alphabetically.
b	jump to the agent that has been blocked longest
B	go back to the session you came from
)	next session (skips ones you have hidden)
(	previous session
u	put back the pane you just closed by accident
E	even out every window on this server
r	rebuild this window's layout
R	rebuild it from the profile, discarding local changes
?	this list
